3	// Native side of the typed Agent bridge. The host owns the runtime
4	// conversation flow, consumes the workspace contract for context, and talks
5	// to the page only through versioned JSON envelopes handed to a send
6	// callback. Conversation and timeline state is document-backed: the
7	// ProjectPersistence document is the durable record, and every mutation goes
8	// through it, so an explicit project save, a reload, or a crash recovery all
9	// reconstruct the same state. GUI-free and deterministic: streaming and tool
10	// execution advance only when the owner calls the pump methods.
11	//
12	// The page renders host state and submits typed requests; it never owns an
13	// editable copy of the conversation or project. Reload reconstruction works
14	// by re-running the handshake: every hello is answered with the complete
15	// state.
